# Playwright e2e

- Discovery: `tests/helpers/fetchAppLinks.ts` crawls the rendered [App Builder](https://shapediver.github.io/GrasshopperExampleModels/11-AppBuilder/definitions.html) and [BETA](https://shapediver.github.io/GrasshopperExampleModels/BETA/definitions.html) pages. Do not parse `definitions.md` — those files are stubs filled from `examples.json` at docs build. Every discovered slug gets smoke + visual tests; `scenarioActions.ts` only adds interactions.
- Scenarios: `tests/config/scenarioActions.ts` — one entry per slug: `params` (e.g. `g` for settings file), `actions(page, slug)` or `namedActions[]` (one Playwright test per name). E-commerce and tools APIs have dedicated specs (`tests/specs/ecommerceApi.spec.ts`, `tests/specs/toolsApi.spec.ts`) so they do not duplicate smoke/visual of `example-executeActions`. Those specs loop a named `actions[]` (one Playwright test per API method).
- Helpers: `viewportCoords` (normalised to the canvas bounding box; canvas starts at **x=300** in the default layout), `waitForModelRecomputed`, `takeSnapshot`, `getParameterElement`, `getStandardContainer` / `setViewportBelowMobileBreakpoint` / `setViewportBelowNavbarBreakpoint` / `openAppShellNavbar` / `expectAppShellNavbarCollapsed` (`tests/helpers/appBuilderContainers.ts`; AppShell `md` is 992px; collapsed navbar uses the `hidden` attribute — Playwright `toBeHidden()` is not reliable because Mantine CSS keeps a layout box). E-commerce and tools e2e both use the localhost parent on `http://127.0.0.1:3000` (`tests/fixtures/cross-window`, iframe `name="app"`). E-commerce: `openCrossWindowScenario`, parent `__connector`. Tools: `openToolsApiScenario` (`?api=tools`), Open agent stubbed to `window.parent` because deployed App Builder sends COOP `same-origin` (a popup to localhost has `window.opener === null`); parent `__toolsApi`. SDV, recompute, and notifications use `sdvTarget(page)` (the iframe). Settings `agentOverride` is a test intercept so Open agent appears; App Builder source is unchanged. `example-ecommerceApi` covers every connector method except `addToCart` (dummy parent rejects after creating a model state). `example-toolsApi` covers every in-scope generic tool. `example-mobileFallback` (`public/example-mobileFallback.json`) covers AppShell theme + JSON overlay + one-hop chain: desktop slots, closed-navbar portrait/landscape layout (leftover `right` in the grid), and open-navbar drawer contents. `example-mobileFallback-grid` (`public/example-mobileFallback-grid.json`) is the same remapping on Grid (no burger; leftover `left` / `right` / `bottom` all on screen). `example-mobileFallback-tabs` covers a tabbed source container and extras landing in a tabbed target’s active tab. `example-mobileFallback-anchors` covers 3d default-to-right vs JSON overlay, 2d theme isolation, and closed-anchor `previewIcon` swap. `example-mobileFallback-keepBottom` covers AppShell `keepBottomInGrid` leftover bottom in the main grid.
- Device: Desktop Chrome, **1280x800**. Mobile-fallback cases resize below `md` (390×844 portrait, 900×700 landscape).
- Deterministic snapshots: `public/example-simple-interaction-colors.json` via `params: {g: ...}` instead of pixel tolerances.
- New behaviours get a scenario entry; models not yet on the test server get the **entry without running it**.

## Deploy / global setup

Global setup deploys root HEAD to `testing/local` via `pnpm run publish` (needs a clean tree, tsc 0, sentry-cli, AWS credentials, `.env`). `SKIP_DEPLOY=1` skips it. A stale local `testing/local` branch **blocks** the deploy.

**Do not deploy or rerun e2e unless the user asks.**
